/*
 * ================================================================
 *  MICROMOUSE 3x3 MAZE SOLVER - AUTONOMOUS (competition) EDITION
 *  No WiFi, no web page. Two pushbuttons and one status LED.
 *  (turning uses ENCODER TICKS ONLY: raw PWM, no gain, no speed loop)
 *  Hardware : ESP32 (Arduino core 3.x) + TB6612FNG + 3x VL53L1X
 *             (Pololu VL53L1X library) + N20 quadrature encoders
 *  Maze     : 3x3 cells. Start (0,0) facing NORTH. Goal: centre (1,1).
 *             x grows to the east, y grows to the north.
 *
 *  BUTTONS (each wired between the pin and GND, internal pull-up is used)
 *   RUN  button (GPIO 23)
 *     short press : robot idle at start  -> EXPLORE & MAP (starts after a short countdown)
 *                   map finished (LED on) -> FINAL RUN     (starts after a short countdown)
 *     press while the robot is moving     -> STOP
 *   BACK button (GPIO 16)
 *     short press : robot carried back to the start, KEEP the map (repeat the final run).
 *                   If there is no finished map yet, it does a reset instead.
 *     long press (1 s) : RESET, wipe the map (start a new exploration)
 *
 *  STATUS LED (GPIO 17, optional, with a resistor to GND)
 *     slow blink = idle / ready      fast blink = running
 *     solid on   = map finished or final run done     very fast blink = error / stopped
 *
 *  USUAL COMPETITION FLOW
 *   1. Place the robot in the start cell facing north. LED slow blink.
 *   2. Press RUN. Take your hand away during the countdown. It explores and returns to the start.
 *   3. LED solid on = map finished. Press RUN again for the fast run to the centre.
 *   4. To run again: carry the robot to the start, press BACK, then RUN.
 *   5. Anything wrong (LED very fast): put the robot at the start, long-press BACK, press RUN.
 *
 *  The USB serial monitor (115200) still works for calibration and debugging, with the same
 *  single-key commands as before (h = help). You do not need it during the competition.
 *
 *  TUNED VALUES
 *   cell = 3677 ticks, 90-degree turn = 1269 ticks, U-turn = 2528 ticks,
 *   left gain 0.941, right gain 0.980 (gains are used for straight driving only)
 *
 *  APPLY_TUNED_ON_BOOT = 1 writes the tuned values into flash at every boot.
 *  FOR THE COMPETITION set it to 0 (so key adjustments you made are kept) and upload again.
 *
 *  SETUP ORDER (serial monitor): k (cell length) -> c (front distance) -> v (motor balance)
 *  NOTE: key v overwrites the gains with measured ones. Skip v to keep 0.941 / 0.980.
 * ================================================================
 */

